{"hash":"982d6fae02eebcd5","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":85.965,"said":"Stand here and look up. Shiva sits above you, about twenty-five metres tall, calm, facing west toward the road and the sea. Keep him in mind: this is a story about why he came. The Shiva Purana tells of a demoness named Daruki and her husband, the demon Daruka. Daruki had worshipped Parvati, and the goddess had given her a boon: this whole forest was placed in her care, and wherever she walked in it, the land grew green and full of trees. But the pair grew proud. With their band of rakshasas they broke up sacrifices and terrorised the people of the forest. The people ran to the sage Aurva for shelter, and he declared: if these demons kill living beings on the earth, they themselves will die. Then the gods came to fight them, and the demons grew afraid. So Daruki called upon her boon. The Purana says she rose and flew like a winged mountain, carrying their city out into the middle of the sea, where the curse could not reach them. But from the water they began to seize the boats that passed. Walk on toward the temple. One of those boats carried a man you should meet.\n\nDid you know? The Shiva Purana places Daruka’s forest on the shore of the western ocean, sixteen yojanas in every direction, one reason devotees here link it with this coast.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1081},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1097,"end":1257}],"words":[[0.098,0.445,0,5],[0.555,0.337,6,10],[0.903,0.204,11,14],[1.12,0.18,15,19],[1.312,0.216,20,22],[2.44,0.385,24,29],[2.837,0.264,30,34],[3.113,0.325,35,40],[3.45,0.276,41,44],[3.954,0.361,46,51],[4.327,0.649,52,63],[4.988,0.445,64,70],[5.445,0.397,71,75],[5.986,0.397,77,81],[6.623,0.493,83,89],[7.127,0.276,90,94],[7.416,0.312,95,101],[7.74,0.072,102,105],[7.824,0.385,106,110],[8.221,0.108,111,114],[8.341,0.084,115,118],[8.438,0.337,119,122],[9.688,0.204,124,128],[9.904,0.168,129,132],[10.084,0.144,133,135],[10.24,0.397,136,140],[10.